 "about_text": "CANDYBAR Gallery is a Kyoto gallery whose name evokes a compact, high-calorie snack bar, chosen to make art feel like an easy, everyday pleasure rather than something intimidating. The gallery's stated aim is to bring beauty into daily routines, encouraging visitors to enjoy 'lucky encounters' with art they love and to imagine the stories behind the works. It opened with a pre-opening sale period in August 2018. Located in the Ygion building near Gion in Higashiyama-ku, its artist roster spans both established Japanese and international postwar and contemporary names, alongside younger Japanese painters and printmakers shown in rotating exhibitions.",
